    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(x)=0$ has no real solutions for any real $k$, so the graph has no $x$-intercepts.\n\nCompleting the square gives $\\Delta=-(k-1)^2-2<0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=-(k^2-2k+1)-2\\\\\\Delta&=-(k-1)^2-2\\leq -2<0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=0$ has no real solutions for any real $k$, and the graph of $y=f(x)$ has no $x$-intercepts. The discriminant alone does not determine the graph's concavity.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
